{
  "_readme": "Default layer, never copied whole. ~/.claude/toolkit-models.json lists only the agents you re-route, in the same shape. Each key under \"agents\" is a shipped toolkit agent name (see plugins/toolkit/agents/*.md). Each value is {\"model\": ..., \"effort\": ...}: model is any Claude Code model alias (\"sonnet\", \"opus\", \"fable\") or a full model ID such as \"claude-opus-5-5\", effort is low, medium, high, xhigh or max. An empty string leaves the layers below in place, and \"inherit\" in either field overrides them and resolves blank. A blank field is not passed on: a Workflow agent() call then inherits the session value, and an Agent-tool spawn with no model uses the agent definition's model, then a configured default subagent model, then the parent session's model. A bare string value is read as the model only. \"haiku\" is refused by the toolkit model policy. This file is the default layer: scripts/resolve-models.sh reads it, then the user file, then the plan note's options, and the result routes Agent-tool spawns through hooks/agent-model.sh and Workflow agent() calls through the runner scripts. An explicit per-call model or effort, or CLAUDE_CODE_SUBAGENT_MODEL_FORCE, wins over every layer.",
